    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.terminals\n\n### Description\n\nHi @echasnovski!\r\n\r\nThanks a lot for mini.nvim, I love the project and use it extensively myself.\r\n\r\nJust raising this issue because I saw that mini.terminals is a planned module. I recently implemented a similar concept for my own personal use, and I would be happy to contribute my implementation as a starting point for the mini.terminals one. You can find it at:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/Charl-AI/dotfiles/blob/main/.config/nvim/lua/repl.lua\r\n\r\nIt is ~150 lines long and is probably the simplest repl/terminals module possible, which I thought would fit in with the ethos of mini.nvim. It supports toggling the inbuilt terminal whilst maintaining its current state, as well as sending visual selections to the terminal.\r\n\r\nI know you like to do things in your own style, so feel free to ignore the suggested implementation or change it however you see fit. Also, if there is anything I can do to help contribute to this module, please let me know how I can help. I just thought it would be a nice opportunity to give back to a project from which I have benefitted.\r\n\r\n:)",
